915:      * A context that keeps information needed during serialization. This context is passed along by
916:      * the methods. In some sense, this replaces the member fields of the class, because the
917:      * serializer is supposed to be "singleton stateless", and because there are multiple instances
918:      * involved (metadata serializer, channel state serializer).
919:      *
920:      * <p>The alternative to passing this context along would be to change the serializers to work
921:      * as actual instances so that they can keep the state. We might still want to do that, but at
922:      * the time of implementing this, it seems the less invasive change to use this context, and it
923:      * also works with static methods and with different serializers instances that do not know of
924:      * each other.
925:      *
926:      * <p>This context is currently hardwired to the FileSystem-based State Backends. At the moment,
927:      * this works because those are the only ones producing relative file paths handles, which are
928:      * in turn the only ones needing this context. In the future, we should refactor this, though,
929:      * and make the DeserializationContext a property of the used checkpoint storage. That makes
930:      */
931:     protected static final class DeserializationContext {
932: 
933:         private final String externalPointer;
934: 
935:         private Path cachedExclusiveDirPath;
