48:  * blocking call. It should be run in the IO executor, not the main thread. The lifecycle is bound
49:  * to single leader election. Once the leadership is revoked, as well as the {@link
50:  * LeaderCallbackHandler#notLeader()} is called, the {@link LeaderElector#run()} will finish. To
51:  * start another round of election, we need to trigger again.
52:  *
53:  * <p>{@link LeaderElector#run()} is responsible for creating the leader ConfigMap and continuously
54:  * update the annotation. The annotation key is {@link #LEADER_ANNOTATION_KEY} and the value is in
55:  * the following json format. metadata: annotations: control-plane.alpha.kubernetes.io/leader:
56:  * '{"holderIdentity":"623e39fb-70c3-44f1-811f-561ec4a28d75","leaseDuration":15.000000000,"acquireTime":"2020-10-20T04:06:31.431000Z","renewTime":"2020-10-22T08:51:36.843000Z","leaderTransitions":37981}'
