818:     /**
819:      * Terminates a TaskManager with the given index.
820:      *
821:      * <p>See {@link #startTaskManager()} to understand how TaskManagers are indexed. This method
822:      * terminates a TaskManager with a given index but it does not clear the index. The index stays
823:      * occupied for the lifetime of the MiniCluster and its TaskManager stays terminated. The index
824:      * is not reused if more TaskManagers are started with {@link #startTaskManager()}.
825:      *
826:      * @param index index of the TaskManager to terminate
827:      * @return {@link CompletableFuture} of the given TaskManager termination
828:      */
829:     public CompletableFuture<Void> terminateTaskManager(int index) {
830:         synchronized (lock) {
831:             final TaskExecutor taskExecutor = taskManagers.get(index);
832:             return taskExecutor.closeAsync();
833:         }
834:     }
